---
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;
---
<TextPage title="Privacy Policy" description="How veronicarivera.design handles your information: what the contact form collects, cookie-free analytics, and your choices."
  eyebrow="Privacy" heading="Privacy Policy"
  lead="This is my personal portfolio. It collects as little as it can, and I never sell or share what it does collect."
  meta="Effective November 8, 2026">
  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>I'm Veronica Rivera, a product designer and design technologist in Louisville, Kentucky. Questions about this policy go to <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>What I collect when you contact me</h2>
  <p>If you send a message through the contact form, it collects:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name</li>
    <li>your email address</li>
    <li>what your message is about</li>
    <li>your message</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I use these only to read and reply to your message.</p>
  <p>The form is run by Formspree. Formspree receives each message, checks it for spam, emails it to me and keeps a copy in my Formspree account. See <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/">Formspree's privacy policy</a>. If you email me directly instead, your message goes to my Gmail account, run by Google.</p>

  <h2>How long I keep messages</h2>
  <p>I keep messages for up to 12 months. Then I delete them from my email and from Formspree.</p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>I use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see how many people visit and which pages they read. It does not use cookies, and it does not follow you to other websites. It records:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>which pages were viewed and how fast they loaded</li>
    <li>the website that sent you here, if any</li>
    <li>your browser, operating system and type of device</li>
    <li>your country</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I can't use it to tell who you are. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and your theme choice</h2>
  <p>This site doesn't use cookies. If you pick Light or Dark in the theme menu, your browser saves that choice so the next page matches. It stays on your device, and you can clear it any time by clearing your browser's site data.</p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like most web hosts, GitHub may keep a short record of visitors' IP addresses to keep the site secure. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.</p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>Some links take you to other websites, like my résumé on Google Docs, my LinkedIn, GitHub, Instagram and TikTok profiles, a news video on YouTube, and the live websites in my case studies. Those sites have their own privacy policies, and this policy doesn't cover them.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site isn't meant for children under 13, and I don't knowingly collect their information. If you think a child has sent me a message, email me and I'll delete it.</p>

  <h2>Keeping your information safe</h2>
  <p>I use trusted services and keep my accounts secure. No website or email service is 100% safe, though, so please don't send passwords or other sensitive details through the form.</p>

  <h2>When I might share information</h2>
  <p>I don't sell, rent or trade your information. I would only share it if the law requires me to.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can ask me what information I have from you, ask me to correct it, or ask me to delete it. Depending on where you live, laws like the GDPR in Europe or the CCPA in California may give you these rights; I'll honor them for everyone. Email <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>, and I'll take care of it within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If I change how this site handles your information, I'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
</TextPage>
